26-10-25 shared-launch instruction (v14).** **v11 driver integrity (Codex rB B3/B4):** the relevant-tree content digest is taken at start, before every spawn and after every cell — any change is PIN DRIFT, exit 4, no further spawns, running cells finish; checkpoints are copied into a content-addressed verified cache `<farm>/.ckpt_cache/<sha>.ckpt` (hash while copying, 0444, atomic rename, free-space gate ≈ 14 GB) and hard-linked into the farm (an existing cache entry must satisfy the immutable contract — regular file, mode 0444, the source's size — and is fully re-hashed at staging AND immediately before EACH spawn; the post-run MEASURED sha256 goes into the receipt; r3c-style symlink farms are refused). **v12 (Codex rB2 B4):** `eval_FLAC.py` reads the checkpoint ONCE into memory, hashes that buffer and deserializes that same buffer (`torch.load(io.BytesIO(buf), map_location='cpu')`, arguments otherwise unchanged), recording `ckpt_sha256_loaded` + `ckpt_bytes_loaded` in every metrics record right after the base keys (records built without it stay byte-identical); `build_receipt` refuses unless loaded == measured == manifest sha and the loaded length == the driver's post-run `stat` (`--ckpt-bytes`); `verify_cell` requires record == receipt for both fields; `--nas-retention-audit` refuses `--dump-check receipt` (rB2 NIT). **Receipt `<stem>.cell.json` (A7, landed):** written only after the post-run full verification; carries the campaign/spawn/post digests, the checkpoint shas (expected + measured + loaded, with the loaded length), `artifact_sha256` of the metrics / `.stream.json` / `.canon.json`, and `dump_evidence` (verified dump manifest sha256, n, shape, dtype, waveform sha256, marker); `verify_cell(dump_check='receipt')` and `gen_model_comparison.py` validate OFFLINE from the committed files; `depth_canon_collect.py --nas-retention-audit` checks the bulk dumps separately. `depth_canon_collect.py`: `verify_cell` (protocol + B2 binding fields per cell class, manifest-level dump check), pairs by (arm, K, seed, step) with the `input_hash` proof, Tier 1 per-position hash equality + recomputed `canonical_depth_hash`, Tier 2 from the dumps via `depth_canon_stats`, Tier 3 (`Δ_C4`, 45° probe, seed-paired `Δ_R` on input_hash-equal pairs only), the table block (mean ± sd, item-weighted and per-scene), TRAJ grid, tie counts per cell and per split, `--partial` labels every heading PARTIAL and lists the missing cells; writes `depth_canon_results.{md,json}`. **Tier-2 control mapping (registered):** 45° → d64, 90° → d128, 180° → d256, 270° → d384, random → random; the pooled control p99 is the reference; matched-offset AND pooled rules plus the 1e-2 cap are all applied (fail-closed reading of "control p99"). The collector accepts as the Tier-2 reference **only** a probe artifact marked `registered: true` (run without `--diagnostic`, sidecar-verified, bound to the CANON@40k checkpoint sha); diagnostic probes are refused (Codex r3b HIGH 4; probe exit codes 0 registered PASS / 1 verdict FAIL / 2 refused / 6 diagnostic); **v11 (Codex rB B5):** a dirty tree is a registered deviation; the collector's `PROBE_CONTRACT` checks the evaluator pin == campaign pin, exact registered arguments, config + split hashes, load protocol, stream census, and renders `eps_cond = v; registered threshold 1e-05: PASS/FAIL` (missing / non-finite ε → artifact invalid). **Pairing (v11, Codex rB NIT):** `context_ids` has exactly K entries per item; strict uniqueness is NOT required because `AR_md` draws with replacement when a room has fewer than K other sources (520 of 6,337 unseen K = 8 targets; identical across the 11 exp_15 streams checked) — the registered rule is that every cell of one (split, K) repeats on the same targets; identical generative noise follows from the execution protocol (same arm/K/step/seed, batch size, census under the pinned evaluator), not from the hash preimage. The shared-map overlap count is derived from the validated audit and compared with the registered 1,093 items / 112 maps. `gen_model_comparison.py` gains the `exp25` contract (rows CANON / P1-pin / YAW-pin at the exp_25 pin, YAW-pin labelled re-measured; validation through `verify_cell`; a round = two-K pair at one pin); additive only.
