/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/fresh_clone_merged/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_2026-10-26_01-08-27_codex_code_rC_review.log-5346-    62	- **CHAIN TRAINING IS LIVE AND SELF-DRIVING** (7,500/40,000 at this entry). **Do not commit anything inside the training closure while legs pend/run** — `train.py`, `defaults.ini`, `src/` except `src/tests`, `data/AR`, the exp_15 kit/configs/helpers. Such a commit aborts the queued leg fail-closed (by design). Worklog/evidence commits are safe and have been made repeatedly during the chain without incident.
/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/fresh_clone_merged/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_2026-10-26_01-08-27_codex_code_rC_review.log-5347-    63	- **Chain recovery is idempotent — never hand-write an `sbatch` for a leg.** If a leg prints `CHAIN STALLED` (classes: 8 banner, 9 audit, 10 smoke, 12 submission, 13 rate breach, 14 terminal record), re-run the exact `yaw_aug_chain_state.py transact-submit` line named in that leg's manifest. It re-reads state under one flock, probes the recorded successor, buries a dead child as a corpse with token rotation, and submits at most one fresh leg. Hand-submitting bypasses the state machine and can fork the chain.
/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/fresh_clone_merged/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_2026-10-26_01-08-27_codex_code_rC_review.log-5348-    64	- **The 2026-08-12 smoke waiver is DISCHARGED.** Its post-hoc obligation (windowed rate floors 0.849/0.843) was evaluated in-chain at leg 1: **PASS, 1.005 steps/s** (`outputs_FLAC/exp15_YAWAUG/yaw_aug_rate_gate.json`) versus VANL's own 0.943 windowed rate. The 30-step smoke's apparent slowdown (0.2 vs 0.37) was a running-average measurement artifact plus node noise, exactly as diagnosed. No open obligation remains from that waiver.
